{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>First instance</b><br>בתורים. Some say [it means] rows of earrings and ornaments of gold, and some say depictions, and they say that it is from [the root of] תאר, and it is called [תורים] because it has no parallel, for [the word תורי] appears only in one book, and it is next to תורי זהב." "נקודות. Like נקודים." "<b>Second instance</b><br>נאוו. Compare [the meaning of נאוו to] the headgear that is on her cheeks like a bit [painted in the form of תורים] on the cheek of horses, and its fastenings with beads on the neck of the horse, and נאוו לך תורי זהב [suits you, rows of gold]."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved the abbreviated ואומ׳ as ואומרים ('and they say'); the passage is elliptical and I have rendered it hyper-literally without smoothing.", 2 "The bracketed phrase [המצוייר בדמות התורי׳] appears to be a gloss inserted into the text; I translate it as presented."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:55.379155477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}